# Line endings are stored exactly as written on disk.
#
# The global git config on this machine sets core.autocrlf=true, which would
# rewrite every text file on commit. Several artifacts here have intentional
# line endings (UTF-16 evidence dumps, generated Markdown/JSON), and the analysis
# toolchain is line-ending agnostic, so normalisation would only add noise to the
# history. The repository therefore pins text=auto off.
* -text

# Explicit binary markers, so no tool ever attempts a text diff on them.
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.pdb binary
*.bin binary
*.unity3d binary
*.clut binary
*.terrain binary
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.zip binary

# Generated artifacts that are committed anyway: keep diffs readable.
*.md text
*.py text
*.js text
*.mjs text
*.json text
*.html text
*.css text
*.cs text
*.ps1 text
*.yml text
*.yaml text
*.tsv text
